  "chunk": "uum with general intelligence: “It was like claiming that the first monkey that\nclimbed a tree was making progress towards landing on the moon” [9]. Deep\nBlue’s chess-playing achievement was indeed hailed as “the first step of an AI\nrevolution” [2], yet such narrow achievements have not translated into broader\nintelligence.\nText-based adventure games present fundamentally different challenges than\nthese well-structured games: they require natural language understanding, com-\nmon sense reasoning about physical objects and spatial relationships, and the\nability to form and test hypotheses about game mechanics [7]. Recent work has\nexplored LLM performance on text-based games with mixed results. Cˆ ot´ e et al.\n[7] introduced TextWorld as a platform for training RL agents on procedurally\ngenerated text games, though most approaches rely on fine-tuning rather than\n3\nzero-shot reasoning. Ammanabrolu and Riedl [1] demonstrated that incorpo-",
